    description: "Found by the 2026-10-05 docstring staleness audit (reviewer reproduced). Repro: A.tla and B.tla each define Init; B.tla's Init body is credited to A.tla's Init (edge A.tla:Init -> B.tla:y), and B.tla:Bar points at A.tla:Init. Same family as the Pony / Pascal / CUDA by-position fixes (WI-rokus, WI-darik, WI-fohuh). Fix: find the enclosing definition by position in the current file (the base class helper), and add a two-file same-name fixture."  # f681
    fields:  # f681
      statement: "A call edge's src is the callable whose body contains the call, found by position in the call's own file (the INV-midag rule the base analyzer follows)."  # f681
      root_cause: "tlaplus.py ~L281 looks up the enclosing operator/theorem/assumption with resolver.lookup(enclosing_name) over the repo-wide resolver instead of the file's own symbols by span."  # f681
